-nature/best-books-about-apollo-program-and-landing-moon-180972653/\', \'content\': \'The story of venturing to the moon does not begin with Apollo, Neil Armstrong or even President John F. Kennedy. Before any human could venture nearly a quarter million miles to another world, the spaceflights of the Mercury program took the first Americans to space, and the Gemini program tested many of the technologies necessary for a lunar voyage, such as docking two spacecraft together and crawling out of a spacecraft in nothing but a pressure suit. Apollo: The Race to the Moon by Charles Murray and Catherine Bly Cox tells this story primarily through the lens of the NASA managers, scientists and engineers who made the moon landing possible. “Murray and Cox provide a ground-level, engineering view of the Mercury, Gemini and Apollo programs,” Neufeld says. “[Their book] paints a vivid [...] The story of venturing to the moon does not begin with Apollo, Neil Armstrong or even President John F. Kennedy. Before any human could venture nearly a quarter million miles to another world, the spaceflights of the Mercury program took the first Americans to space, and the Gemini program tested many of the technologies necessary for a lunar voyage, such as docking two spacecraft together and crawling out of a spacecraft in nothing but a pressure suit. Apollo: The Race to the Moon by Charles Murray and Catherine Bly Cox tells this story primarily through the lens of the NASA managers, scientists and engineers who made the moon landing possible. “Murray and Cox provide a ground-level, engineering view of the Mercury, Gemini and Apollo programs,” Neufeld says. “[Their book] paints a vivid [...] Earthrise: How Man First Saw the Earth by Robert Poole, a former editor at Smithsonian, explores the significance of this photo and other images of Earth taken from space. Filled with beautiful pictures and stories from missions to the moon, the book delves into the impact of the Apollo program on everything from environmentalism to religion to science. “Poole’s story is one of ancient and academic ideas of the moon and the Earth, and how astronaut photographs like Earthrisefrom Apollo 8 became a primary means by which people would fulfill dreams of lunar travel and come to realize the scientific reality of the Earth-moon system,” says Jennifer Levasseur, a curator in the Smithsonian’s National Air and Space Museum’s space history department.\', \'score\': 0.99361163}, {\'title\': \'Moon Landing by Stephen Krensky\', \'url\': \'https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/812345/moon-landing-by-stephen-krensky/\', \'content\': \'Listen With the Whole Family\\n\\nView All  >\\n\\nNew Stories to Listen to\\n10 Audiobook Originals You Need To Hear\\nsearch\\nPenguin Random House\\nPenguin Random House\\nPenguin Random House\\nSign In\\nsearch\\nclose search\\nclose search\\nMoon Landing by Stephen Krensky\\n\\n# Moon Landing\\n\\nThe Incredible Story of the Apollo 11 Mission\\n\\n## By Stephen KrenskyRead by René Valius\\n\\n### Age Range: 9-12 years\\n\\nMoon Landing by Stephen Krensky\\n\\nBuy from Other Retailers:\\n\\nPublished on Mar 24, 2026 | 2 Hours\\n\\nBuy from Other Retailers:\\n\\n### Book Description\\n\\n#### Related Genres\\n\\n### Product Details\\n\\nISBN9798217139675\\n\\nPublished onMar 24, 2026\\n\\nPublished byDK Children\\n\\nLength2 Hours\\n\\nAge Range9-12 years\\n\\nGradeGrades 4-7\\n\\nAuthor\\n\\nStephen Krensky [...] ### Who Was Cleopatra?\\n\\nQUICK VIEW\\nAdd Who Is "Weird Al" Yankovic? to bookshelf\\nBook cover\\n\\n### Who Is “Weird Al” Yankovic?\\n\\nAdd Who Is Jenna Ortega? to bookshelf\\nBook cover\\n\\n### Who Is Jenna Ortega?\\n\\nAdd ¡Viva Valenzuela! to bookshelf\\nBook cover\\n\\n### ¡Viva Valenzuela!\\n\\nAdd World Soccer Kings to bookshelf\\nBook cover\\n\\n### World Soccer Kings\\n\\nAdd Sports: How to Draw Books for Kids to bookshelf\\nBook cover\\n\\n### Sports: How to Draw Books for Kids\\n\\nAdd Moon Landing to bookshelf\\nB