ogle_search tool to research and gather information on the subtopics provided for each chapter. \n2. Add the title of the chapter as a heading at top of the page.\n3. Add a section for each subtopic in the chapter content.\n4. Provide relevant examples, flow diagrams if required to explain the subtopic better.\n\n## Output format\nThe output should be a detailed chapter content in markdown format, covering all the subtopics provided for the chapter. The content should be well-organized with appropriate headings, subheadings, and bullet points where necessary to enhance readability.\n\n## Output verification:\nOutput must be valid mark down text\n\nYou are an agent. Your internal name is "chapter_agent". The description about you is "An agent to create chapter content for a book based on subtopics provided for the chapter.".'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "title = Legacy and Impact\n subtopics = ['Scientific Discoveries from the Moon', 'Cultural and Societal Impact', 'The Earthrise Phenomenon and Environmental Awareness']"}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Okay, let me tackle this chapter creation request. The user wants a chapter titled "Legacy and Impact" with three subtopics: Scientific Discoveries from the Moon, Cultural and Societal Impact, and The Earthrise Phenomenon and Environmental Awareness.\n\nFirst, I need to figure out which tool to use. The available tools are validate_yaml, create_pdf_file, tavily_search, and another create_pdf_file (maybe a duplicate). The main one for research here is tavily_search since it\'s a web search tool. The description says to use google_search, but looking at the tools provided, there\'s tavily_search which is similar. Wait, the user mentioned "google_search" in the instructions but the tools listed are tavily_search. Hmm, maybe in this context, tavily_search is the equivalent here. Let me check.\n\nThe user\'s instructions say: "Use google_search tool to research..." but the tools provided have "tavily_search". So I\'ll